00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.849
Next post.

00:01:53.849 --> 00:01:56.099
What exactly is this open border?

00:01:56.099 --> 00:01:57.509
Does anyone know this argument?

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:01.889
We've all heard conservatives point to this
crazy, unruly open border.

00:02:01.889 --> 00:02:03.229
That's Biden's fault.

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:04.709
What changed at the border?

00:02:04.709 --> 00:02:08.489
I've never seen the U.S. under any president,
have an open border, and I don't understand

00:02:08.489 --> 00:02:09.599
the argument.

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:12.280
Aren't we still deporting people and turning
them away?

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:15.540
Isn't the process to get citizenship highly
complex and lengthy?

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.870
I always hear people say we have an open border
and we give immigrants money, health care

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:20.870
and education.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.870
Where exactly is that happening?

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.180
Is this all made up, or is there some factual
basis for the claim?

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:30.250
So the truth is there has been nothing, and
it's actually mentioned in a comment in this

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.500
Reddit post.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.730
We've had nothing approximating an open border
of any kind for about 100 years.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.390
There are countries that do.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:44.430
Although I'm not up to exactly where it stands
right now, my birth country of Argentina for

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.430
a long time.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:49.069
I'm not going to say it's exactly this way
now because I'm not sure, but for a long time,

00:02:49.069 --> 00:02:53.459
anyone could basically go and assuming that
within, I don't remember it was a year or

00:02:53.459 --> 00:02:54.459
two.

00:02:54.459 --> 00:03:00.099
You either are able to get enrolled in a university
or are able to find a job.

00:03:00.099 --> 00:03:03.080
That's your path to legal status in Argentina
now.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.260
It's not like Argentina is the U.S. and everybody's
trying to go to Argentina.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.840
Not that everybody's trying to go to the U.S.,
but there's a lot more people trying to come

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.850
to the U.S. than to go to Argentina.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.239
But no, the post is right.

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:14.390
There is not an open border.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:20.960
Even the process for requesting asylum is
not a particularly short or easy process.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:25.959
There is no open border, and it's just another
one of these vapid right wing talking points

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:28.889
that works on a lot of people.

